  "body": "﻿## What changed\r\n\r\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_depth.rs`: new `picked_law`. A picked ring that walks no level below the local part top is refused by name when the operation levels go below that top. The local top is the highest vertex of the facets near the ring (XY box plus the tool radius and the stock to leave).\r\n- `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour.rs`: new entry point `contour_on_picked`. It runs the law after the depth ladder. `contour_on_part` and `contour_on_bodies` do not change.\r\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`: the Selection source of 2D Contour calls `contour_on_picked`. The whole-model source (entity or stock) does not change.\r\n- `docs/decisions/1927-contour-picked-ring-law.md`: the decision and the dropped alternatives.\r\n\r\nThe refusal text names the ring position, the part top and the fix, for example: \"the picked ring at (0.294, -12.986) meets its wall at no level below the part top Z 10.000: the cutter Outside this ring stands in the part material - if the ring bounds a hole, set Side to Inside; else check the tool containment\". The side that the law reads is the resolved side (the app resolves Auto first), and a tool containment also moves the ring. Thus the text names the two causes.\r\n\r\nTwo existing tests pinned the silent top-plane pass and change:\r\n- `crates/app/tests/area_open.rs`: on the rim of a blind bore, Side Auto resolves to Outside, and a forced Containment Outside puts the ring 10 mm into the wall. The two cases cut only the mouth, in air, with 0 warnings. They are now refused by name. Side Inside is the clean control. The test is renamed to `a_containment_that_puts_the_tool_in_the_part_is_refused_by_name`. The wrong Auto verdict on blind bores is #1933 (P3). This PR does not fix it.\r\n- `crates/app/tests/tilt.rs`: the flat control used Inside on the top face of a block (the mirror case). It now uses Outside.\r\n\r\n## Readings (main `d1484f02a`)\r\n\r\n- Plate 60 x 60 x [0, 10], through hole D20, D6 end mill, stepdown 2.5.\r\n- Side Outside on the hole wall walked only Z 10 and posted with status Ok, 0 warnings and 0 gouges. Full depth (Bottom of model) gave the same result.\r\n- Cause: the depth ladder reads the material strictly above each level. At the part top no material is above, so each ring is legal there.\r\n- The tip stayed on the top face, so the posted path did not gouge. It machined nothing that the user picked and said nothing.\r\n- `verify` on the same ring forced down the full ladder reports Gouge warnings. The verifier has no gap, so no verifier issue is filed.\r\n- Details are in the issue comment.\r\n\r\n## Pinning tests\r\n\r\n`crates/app/tests/contour_outside_hole.rs` (5 tests):\r\n\r\n- `outside_on_a_picked_hole_wall_is_refused_by_name_at_every_depth` (chain pick and patch pick, full depth and selection heights)\r\n- `inside_and_auto_on_the_hole_wall_cut_every_level_clean`\r\n- `outside_on_an_outer_wall_and_on_a_boss_stays_legal`\r\n- `inside_on_a_picked_block_top_is_refused_by_name`\r\n- `the_full_depth_outside_ring_is_a_gouge_to_the_verifier`\r\n\r\nAlso pinned: `area_open::a_containment_that_puts_the_tool_in_the_part_is_refused_by_name`, `tilt::tilt_on_a_picked_selection_refuses_by_name`.\r\n\r\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick`) on `dfceb20ac`: post suites ok (67 s), motion suites ok (777 s), app suites ok (775 s), 0 failed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean. `cargo fmt --check` is clean. The branch has a merge of `origin/main` (it takes the #1924 test repair). The last commit is docs only.\r\n\r\n## Review fix (head 72c8f293d)\n\nA quick gate on a tree with 0761173e8 had two red camcraft-app tests. On origin/main they cannot fail this way: the refusal text is not in main (`git grep` finds 0 hits).\n\n- `setup_align::unverified_kinds_are_refused_while_verified_picks_generate_aligned`: the refusal is correct. The test picked the first horizontal face, the modelled top annulus (Z 20, hole 20 x 20). The setup flips the part over Y, so the annulus lies at the setup's Z 0 and the blind hole opens down (Z 0..10). Z 10..20 is solid 40 x 40. Outside of the hole ring, the cutter centre runs at +-8 mm, in that solid at Z 16 and Z 12. The old path kept only the top plane, in air. The law reads the setup frame: the same ring generates as modelled. The test now picks the modelled bottom face (the setup's top) with Side Outside and asserts a cut below Z 19.9. The annulus stays as a control: it generates as modelled and is refused by name after the flip. The Offset2D refusal and the Contour1 assert do not change.\n- `stitch_cross::a_self_touching_single_body_still_stops_at_its_top_level`: the refusal gave the wrong cause. The ring is Outside of a 40 x 40 outline, and Outside is air. The ladder stopped the ring at Z 10 because the one self-touching shell cannot be sectioned at Z 0 (non-manifold slice error, fail closed). The law said \"set Side to Inside\", which is wrong advice. Fix: `contour_depth::ladder` keeps the slice error that stopped each ring (`Ladder::unread`). `picked_law` still refuses, but it names that error and the skipped levels, and does not name the side. The test asserts the refusal, `levels below skipped (0.000)`, `non-manifold`, and no Side advice. The one-block reference still cuts below the top.\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`) on 72c8f293d: motion suites ok (843 s), app suites ok (785 s), setup_align and stitch_cross ok, 0 failed. Targeted runs: stitch_cross 6/6, setup_align 10/10, contour_outside_hole 5/5, area_open 11/11, tilt 8/8, operations 120/120 (6 ignored). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean. `cargo fmt --check` was not run on this head: `cargo fmt -p` fails with os error 206 on this machine.\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The MCP path and the GUI (the same generator runs under them).\r\n- Multi-body picks with bodies of different heights.\r\n- Auto on a blind bore is pinned as a refusal only (#1933 owns the verdict).\r\n- The release lanes.\r\n\r\n`contour.rs` was 446 lines before this PR (over the 400-line law). This PR adds 15 lines. A split is owed separately.\r\n\r\nChangelog: 2D Contour refuses a picked ring whose side lies in the part at each level (Outside on a hole wall, Inside on a block outline), with the fix in the message. Before, it cut only the top plane and posted with no warning.\r\n\r\nEffort: high\r\n\r\nFixes #1927\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\n\r\n",
